From e27f73cc5f997cd501c17c4d5c125ccf5bbc36b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mitzev <ogi@kunasystems.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 20:57:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.39: ItemKind::Class AST variant (1.01 #7)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Promotes the fork-only `class` keyword from parse-time desugar
(P09.30) to a first-class AST variant that survives through name
resolution and lowers at AST → HIR with proper DefId separation.

This is the compiler-internal enabler for 1.02's rust-analyzer
fork: RA's parser can mirror rustc's AST shape instead of
duplicating the desugaring logic. No user-visible change on its
own — v1 probes (basic class, single inheritance, Swift bindings)
all still run green.

Design (Option B1): parser emits `ItemKind::Class(Box<Class>)`
carrying ident, generics, fields, methods, impl_id (NodeId
reserved for the synthetic inherent impl), and self_ty (an AST
path to ClassIdent<Args> used as the impl's self type). The
`#[repr(cpp)]` attr still lands on the enclosing Item's attrs
at parse time; it propagates to the struct half via normal
`lower_item` attribute plumbing.

AST → HIR: `AstOwner` gains a `ClassImpl` variant so the impl
half gets its own `lower_node` dispatch. `lower_item_ref`
emits two ItemIds per Class. `lower_item_kind` Class arm
produces the struct half. `lower_class_impl_half` produces the
inherent impl half, using `lower_ty` on the parser-built
`self_ty` to get a correctly resolved self type.

Name resolution: `resolve_class` delegates to `resolve_adt` —
one generic-param rib and one self-rib cover both fields and
methods because the class's generics are shared.
`def_collector` creates two defs per class (struct at
`item.id`, impl at `class.impl_id`) and walks methods under
the impl def so assoc items get the right parent.
`build_reduced_graph_for_item` registers the struct-variant
names and feeds visibility for both defs.

Miscellaneous:
- rustc_passes/lang_items: Class methods classify as
  MethodKind::Inherent (matches HIR shape post-lowering)
- rustc_passes/input_stats: Class added to variant list
- rustc_hir/target: Target::Struct for Class at AST level
- rustc_ast_pretty: new arm prints class with fields + methods
- visit.rs: walks impl_id through visit_visitable! so
  `rustc_expand::expand`'s `visit_id` replaces the parser's
  DUMMY_NODE_ID with a fresh NodeId

Removed from P09.30:
- Parser::pending_injected_item field (Parser size back to 288)
- parse_item's pending-item return path
- parse_cxx_class_item's hand-built Impl Item construction

Validation: stage-1 rustc builds clean; rustcc workspace
`cargo test --workspace` = 235/0; /tmp/p09-39-itemkind-class
probe covers basic class + single inheritance with
`Derived::sum() == 15`.
